D('sections',1,'Track a job from receipt to a checked result','Count accepted work, completed work and deliveries separately.',[g('Learning goals',[1,2,3]),g('Retrieve identifiers and committed-result recovery',[i for i in range(5,ready) if a.w['sections'][0]['blocks'][i].get('text','').startswith(('Close your','Without opening','After trying'))]),g('Prerequisite and starting response',[ready+1,ready+2],'prompts'),g('End goal',[end+1])])
intro=a.add('sections',2,'Imagine handing a library card to a helper. A receipt means the request was accepted; it does not mean the book is ready. A queue works similarly: it holds jobs for a worker. Keep the same job ID when work is delivered again. Before repeating an effect, consult reliable saved completion evidence. A completed result can be returned again without doing the effect again; uncertain status requires reconciliation.')
