p=a.add('sections',6,image=a.pic(2));ch=a.add('sections',6,image=a.pic(4));scope=a.add('sections',6,'The picture uses queued/running/succeeded/failed; the main example uses pending/running/completed/failed. Queued corresponds to pending and succeeded to completed for these classroom cases. J12’s submission receipt acknowledges acceptance, not the worker’s later delivery completion. Only checked output permits succeeded. If a supervisor observes and records a crash before checked output, failed is justified; a declared retry could return it to queued. If nobody has yet observed the crash, the saved status may remain running and needs reconciliation. Do not invent a success, an observed failure or a retry policy from the mere absence of output.')
