lab=a.add('sections',9,'Predict J’s state and effect count at acceptance, after commit/crash and on redelivery. The main path has two modeled deliveries and one mock effect. A copied saved snapshot lets a new worker return the previous result with no new effect. Unknown IDs and running-only snapshots go to review; changed payload under J is rejected. A separate lost-history demonstration repeats the mock effect, exposing the memory-only limitation. The J12 picture records an observed pre-output failure. This synchronous program creates no real queue, durable record, conversion or external effect; its single commit step assumes the atomic relationship a real system would need to implement. Record “not run” for a paper trace.')
