t=a.add('teacher',2,image=a.w['sections'][1]['blocks'][policy]);le=a.add('teacher',2,image=a.w['sections'][2]['blocks'][ledger]);pr=a.add('teacher',2,image=a.w['sections'][6]['blocks'][probes]);sp=a.add('teacher',2,a.w['sections'][5]['blocks'][scope]['text']);tp=a.add('teacher',2,image=a.pic(2));key=a.add('teacher',2,'Main J is committed before the crash, so the reliable completion record permits returning its prior result on redelivery and acknowledging without another effect: two deliveries, one mock effect. A running or unknown record does not justify replay; reconcile first. Same-ID changed payload is a conflict. Submission acceptance and worker acknowledgement are different signals. Picture J12 is queued at receipt and succeeded only after checked output. An observed pre-output crash can be recorded failed; an unobserved crash may leave running status. The code represents commit as one sequential step and copies a supplied snapshot; it proves no durable storage, external-effect atomicity, concurrency policy or exactly-once delivery. Losing history demonstrates the limitation. Do not reveal the selected three-job answer while modelling.')
D('teacher',2,'Teach acceptance, completion evidence and redelivery separately','Explicitly contrast the main post-commit crash with the pictured pre-output crash.',[g('Definitions and complete classroom state contract',[0,2,t]),g('Main event ledger and checked reasoning',[le,key,5,6,9,10,11]),g('Conflict, uncertainty and lost-history probes',[pr],'example'),g('Separate J12 vocabulary and observation qualification',[15,17,sp]),g('Picture trace and crash key',[tp,19,21,23,25,26,27])])
ref='A queue separates accepting work from completing it. Main states are pending, running, completed and failed. Picture vocabulary queued/succeeded corresponds to pending/completed. A submission receipt proves acceptance; a worker acknowledgement is a separate signal after the declared durable completion step. Main job J commits a checked result then crashes before acknowledgement. Redelivery with the same ID and payload consults reliable completion evidence, returns the prior result and acknowledges without another effect: two deliveries, one mock effect. Unknown or running-only status requires reconciliation; same-ID changed payload is a conflict. Separate J12 receipt proves queued only; checked output permits succeeded. An observed pre-output crash permits failed status, while an unobserved crash may leave stale running status. No retry policy is implied. Reliable effect/status correspondence is an explicit assumption. The code is sequential in-memory fiction with copied snapshots; it implements no broker, durable commit, concurrency or exactly-once delivery. Losing history can lead to a repeated mock effect.'
a.references('the selected accepted/completed/failed/pending three-job case','Main J redelivery returns its prior committed result and adds zero effects; the original commit remains the one mock effect across two deliveries. Unknown/running status needs reconciliation and changed-payload ID reuse is rejected. Picture J12 receipt is not conversion success; an observed pre-output crash is failed, while an unobserved crash may leave stale running status. Selected independent jobs A/B/C: one completed, one failed, one pending; all three were accepted but all-success is false. Require the three state counts, not just a total accepted count.',ref)
